# Migrations: forward-only (#193)

- From `1.0.0-beta.1` on, every schema change is a **new migration**. Never edit, rename or delete an existing file in `database/migrations/`. The old pre-release rule (edit the `create_*` migrations in place) no longer applies.
- A new migration runs with `php artisan migrate --force` on a customer database that has data: backfill what it needs, never assume `migrate:fresh`. It must work on SQLite, MySQL and PostgreSQL (CI runs all three).
- Index the columns of hot queries and every foreign key column (PostgreSQL does not index them); `tests/Feature/SchemaTest.php` checks the foreign keys and the cascade on project delete.
- CI `migrations-frozen / migrations-frozen` (app-ui's shared `migrations-frozen.yml`) fails when a PR modifies or deletes a migration that exists on `main`, on the latest `v*` tag or in `database/migrations/.frozen`. That baseline only grows: never remove or change a line.
